## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates building a pluggable scheduling system where policies evolve without changing the core orchestrator. Focus on isolation, runtime extensibility, and safe concurrent access.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern for interchangeable scheduling algorithms
- Registry pattern for runtime policy registration
- Thread-safe, lazy-loaded registry and policy implementations
- Handling of job metadata for policy selection

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Job {
  id: string
  priority: number
  deadline?: Date
  resources?: any
}

interface SchedulingPolicy {
  pickNext(jobs: Job[]): Job | null;
}

class PolicyRegistry {
  private policies = new Map<string, SchedulingPolicy>();

  register(name: string, policy: SchedulingPolicy): void {
    this.policies.set(name, policy);
  }

  get(name: string): SchedulingPolicy | undefined {
    return this.policies.get(name);
  }
}

// FIFO Policy
class FIFOPolicy implements SchedulingPolicy {
  pickNext(jobs: Job[]): Job | null {
    return jobs.length > 0 ? jobs[0] : null;
  }
}

// Priority Policy
class PriorityPolicy implements SchedulingPolicy {
  pickNext(jobs: Job[]): Job | null {
    return jobs.sort((a, b) => b.priority - a.priority)[0] || null;
  }
}

// Usage
const registry = new PolicyRegistry();
registry.register('fifo', new FIFOPolicy());
registry.register('priority', new PriorityPolicy());

const policy = registry.get('priority');
const nextJob = policy?.pickNext(jobQueue);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design extensible components with runtime plug-ins, and to coordinate parallel I/O with clear error reporting.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern: pluggable channels
- Registry for runtime extensibility
- Promise.all or allSettled for parallel delivery
- Uniform per-channel error shape and per-channel isolation

## Code Example
```typescript
export interface Channel { send(msg: string, meta?: any): Promise<void> }
export type ChannelFactory = () => Channel
export class ChannelRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, ChannelFactory>()
  register(name: string, factory: ChannelFactory) { this.map.set(name, factory) }
  create(name: string): Channel { const f = this.map.get(name); if (!f) throw new Error(`Unknown channel: ${name}`); return f() }
}

export class Notifier {
  constructor(private registry: ChannelRegistry) {}
  async notify(msg: string, channels: string[]) {
    const tasks = channels.map(n => {
      try { return this.registry.create(n).send(msg) } catch (e) { return Promise.reject(e) }
    })
    const results = await Promise.allSettled(tasks)
    return results.map((r, idx) => ({ channel: channels[idx], ok: r.status === 'fulfilled', error: r.status === 'rejected' ? (r.reason as Error).message : undefined }))
  }
}
```

